# EY Design System & Tokens (Required)

Every UI implementation must use the EY design kit. Do not invent colors, spacing, or type styles.

## Canonical sources

| Concern | Source |
|---------|--------|
| JS tokens | `src/design-kit/tokens.ts` (`colors`, `fonts`, `typeScale`, `spacing`, `layout`) |
| CSS vars | `src/styles/theme.css` (`var(--foreground)`, `var(--ey-content-width)`, etc.) |
| Type UI | `src/design-kit/EYTypography.tsx` |
| Kit entry | `import { colors, fonts, typeScale, spacing, layout, contentRailStyle, EYHeading, EYBody } from '@/design-kit'` |

Read `src/DESIGN.md` before building new UI. Prefer existing kit components (`EYButton`, `EYCard`, `EYFrame`, etc.) over one-off styles.

## Color

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — raw hex / Tailwind palette
style={{ color: '#2E2E38' }}
className="bg-blue-500 text-gray-800"

// ✅ GOOD — tokens or CSS vars
import { colors } from '@/design-kit';
style={{ color: colors.offBlack, background: colors.offWhite }}
style={{ color: 'var(--foreground)', background: 'var(--card)' }}
```

- EY Yellow (`colors.yellow` / `var(--ey-brand-yellow)`) is a **marker/accent only** — never body text on white, never large decorative fills.
- Prefer `var(--*)` in CSS/Tailwind theme classes; prefer `colors.*` in inline React styles.

## Typography

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
style={{ fontFamily: 'Inter', fontSize: 18, fontWeight: 500 }}

// ✅ GOOD
import { fonts, typeScale } from '@/design-kit';
// or <EYHeading>, <EYBody>, <EYEyebrow> from the kit
style={{
  fontFamily: fonts.regular,
  fontSize: typeScale.body.size,
  fontWeight: typeScale.body.weight,
}}
```

- Font: **EYInterstate** only (via `fonts.bold` / `fonts.regular` / `fonts.light`).
- Weights allowed: **300 / 400 / 700** only (no 500/600).

## Spacing & content width (global)

**Content rail is a single token.** Default `layout.contentWidth = '80%'`. Change that one value in `src/design-kit/tokens.ts` — `main.tsx` writes it to `--ey-content-width`, so all pages update.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hardcoded rails
style={{ maxWidth: 1200, margin: '0 auto' }}
style={{ padding: '72px 64px' }}

// ✅ GOOD — tokenized rail
import { layout, contentRailStyle, spacing, contentInlinePad } from '@/design-kit';
<div style={contentRailStyle}>...</div>
<section style={{ padding: spacing.sectionPadding }}>...</section>
// or CSS: width: var(--ey-content-width); className="ey-content-rail"
```

- Section **backgrounds** stay full-bleed; only the **content** sits in the rail
- Do not invent `maxWidth: 1100/1200` wrappers — use `contentRailStyle` or `var(--ey-content-width)`
- Side inset helper: `contentInlinePad` / `var(--ey-content-inline-pad)`

## Icons (line only)

All icons must be **line / stroke icons** from `lucide-react` (or an equivalent inline SVG with `fill="none"` + `stroke="currentColor"`).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — emoji or filled/pictorial icons in CTAs, labels, nav
<a>Let's Start with the Fundamentals👇</a>

// ✅ GOOD — Lucide line icon beside the label
import { ArrowDown } from 'lucide-react';
<a className="paths-cta" href="#evolution">
  Let's Start with the Fundamentals
  <ArrowDown size={16} strokeWidth={1.75} aria-hidden />
</a>
```

- Never use emoji as UI icons (👇 ➡️ ✅ etc.)
- Prefer outline Lucide icons; do not use filled/solid icon sets
- In raw HTML lessons, use a small stroke SVG matching Lucide (16–20px), not emoji
- Icon color inherits via `currentColor` from the parent text/token color

## Checklist before shipping UI

1. No hardcoded hex/rgba except inside `tokens.ts` / `theme.css`
2. No Tailwind color utilities (`bg-blue-*`, `text-gray-*`, `text-[#…]`)
3. Text uses kit fonts + `typeScale` or `EYTypography` components
4. Spacing comes from `spacing` or matching existing kit patterns
5. Icons are Lucide (or Lucide-equivalent) line strokes — never emoji
6. Content rails use `layout.contentWidth` / `contentRailStyle` / `var(--ey-content-width)` — never hardcoded `maxWidth: 1100/1200`
